1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
(Episode 3)

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,690
This city is my one true love.

3
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:09,890
I'm going to take everything for myself.

4
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:12,990
And anyone who dares get in my way...

5
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:16,150
I'll kill them.

6
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,660
I'm begging you.

7
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:22,570
Please save the Kirii-gumi.

8
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:30,270
What would you do if
something happened to me?

9
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:34,610
I won't let that happen.

10
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:37,870
This time, I'll protect you no matter what.

11
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:40,970
Dead or alive, we're in this together.

12
00:00:45,910 --> 00:00:48,030
Come to think of it, I
don't think I ever told you...

13
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:50,390
why I married you in the first place.

14
00:00:54,810 --> 00:00:56,330
I'll tell you once we get back.

15
00:00:58,150 --> 00:00:59,150
Ren.

16
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:15,610
O-Odajima!

17
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:25,240
Ren-Ren... No, wait.

18
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:26,920
Odajima-san!

19
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,040
Are you okay?

20
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:29,080
Go after them!

21
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,880
- But... - Just go!

22
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:49,550
A kidnapping, huh?

23
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:51,570
Brings back memories.

24
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:54,230
I used to have my guys pull
this kind of thing all the time.

25
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:56,670
Still, I'd much rather be
having lunch right now.

26
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:02,160
Come on, give me a smile.

27
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,120
Don't leave me hanging
here, it's embarrassing.

28
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:07,510
So...

29
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:10,670
where are you guys taking me?

30
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
The Journey To Killing You Season 2.

31
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,990
Yeah, I went after
them, but I lost the tail...

32
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:35,910
I'm really sorry!

33
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:37,330
Excuse me.

34
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:43,930
Are you holding up okay?

35
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:45,470
Hold on.

36
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:46,850
Odajima-san.

37
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:48,590
It's too dangerous.

38
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,590
Hey, wait up!

39
00:03:56,690 --> 00:03:59,096
- Did you sell him out?
- What the hell are you talking about?

40
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,290
Kataoka-san.

41
00:04:01,170 --> 00:04:02,626
He was snatched right off the street.

42
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:03,800
Who did you sell him to?

43
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,370
Are you out of your mind?

44
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,720
I owe his old man a
huge debt from way back.

45
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,630
If anything, you guys...

46
00:04:14,830 --> 00:04:16,580
were already being tailed, weren't you?

47
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:23,890
The only ones bold enough to
pull a kidnapping around here...

48
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,930
are VOID.

49
00:04:27,490 --> 00:04:28,490
VOID?

50
00:04:31,110 --> 00:04:32,350
You know, that gang of punks...

51
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,920
giving your Kirii-gumi such a
massive headache in Awakuma.

52
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:46,490
Please, wait!

53
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:48,370
Those VOID guys are bad news.

54
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,920
They play dirty. If we
make a reckless move,

55
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:52,439
Kataoka-san might...

56
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,030
never make it back alive!

57
00:04:55,610 --> 00:04:56,610
I'm begging you!

58
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,640
Let's talk this over with
Boss Kumakura first.

59
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:01,810
Please!

60
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:18,950
Well, this is a real mess.

61
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,910
Why the hell would those VOID punks...

62
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:27,490
What's our move?

63
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:33,510
Stay away from them.

64
00:05:34,850 --> 00:05:36,590
Then what about Kataoka-san?

65
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,160
Hey.

66
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:41,870
What happened to that bastard Kataoka?

67
00:05:44,590 --> 00:05:45,790
Boss...

68
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,820
Isn't this a luxury hotel?

69
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,760
Bet they've got an
open-air hot spring, too.

70
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,420
What are you doing here?

71
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,560
Where's Kataoka?

72
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,300
Did you two break up?

73
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,760
No.

74
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,920
I was the one who asked them to come.

75
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:48,020
Huh?

76
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,700
I wanted to ask Kataoka...

77
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,900
to help save the Kirii-gumi...

78
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,480
from this crisis.

79
00:06:57,780 --> 00:06:58,880
You asked Kataoka?

80
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,320
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

81
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,820
You expect me to beg that guy for help?

82
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,040
I am deeply sorry.

83
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,920
But right now...

84
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,540
this is an emergency.

85
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Kataoka...

86
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,560
has been taken.

87
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:22,620
I'm afraid VOID is behind it.

88
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,320
That's none of our business.

89
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,060
Get out.

90
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:11,480
Odajima-san!

91
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,080
Please, let me come with you.

92
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,500
Appreciate it!

93
00:08:37,010 --> 00:08:38,600
Quite the warm welcome you've got here.

94
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,720
Makes me wanna pop a bottle
of champagne to celebrate.

95
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:48,140
Hey, it's rude to ignore people, you know.

96
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:37,740
Odajima-san?

97
00:09:40,030 --> 00:09:41,570
Are you guys with VOID?

98
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,840
Where is Kataoka-san?!

99
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:43,780
Who the hell does this guy think he is?

100
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:45,070
Hey, what's your problem, man?

101
00:09:48,450 --> 00:09:50,500
- Odajima-san! - Let go!

102
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,720
Where is Kataoka-san?!

103
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,050
Hey, let's bounce.

104
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:58,920
Hold it!

105
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,590
- Stop! - Don't run!

106
00:10:07,730 --> 00:10:08,730
Damn it!

107
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,600
Stop right there!

108
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:13,500
Get back here!

109
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:14,960
Hey! Stop!

110
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,380
- Cut them off! - Got it!

111
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,029
Hey! Freeze!

112
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:56,030
Hey!

113
00:10:57,040 --> 00:11:00,160
No, don't! It's too dangerous!

114
00:11:00,270 --> 00:11:02,450
Calm down, Ren-Ren.

115
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:37,330
What's that awful smell?

116
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:40,860
Don't tell me...

117
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,349
Whoa! Whoa!

118
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:52,060
A stinkbug! Ugh, it's a stinkbug!

119
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,060
Hey! There's a stinkbug in here! Hey!

120
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:17,110
Ahhh!

121
00:12:21,650 --> 00:12:25,120
Ugh, it reeks!

122
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:14,210
Wait, could this van be...

123
00:13:18,050 --> 00:13:19,050
Odajima!

124
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:29,590
What do yakuza want around here?

125
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:32,479
Where's the owner of this van?

126
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:35,480
Is it owned by some young guy?

127
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:38,510
Whoa, demanding answers right off the bat?

128
00:13:39,310 --> 00:13:40,510
That's private information.

129
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:42,530
I can't just hand that over to you.

130
00:13:45,850 --> 00:13:46,950
Huh?

131
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:49,270
Wait, aren't you...

132
00:13:51,150 --> 00:13:52,150
Ren-Ren?

133
00:13:55,130 --> 00:13:57,660
I knew it! It is Ren-Ren!

134
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:58,950
Man, oh man.

135
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,240
I almost didn't recognize
you without the aloha shirt.

136
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:05,290
KinRen.

137
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:08,030
I watch your channel, you know.

138
00:14:09,730 --> 00:14:11,820
Okinawa looked like a blast.

139
00:14:14,050 --> 00:14:15,050
And Kin-Kin...

140
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,430
Speaking of young Kataoka...

141
00:14:18,270 --> 00:14:19,270
Oh...

142
00:14:19,850 --> 00:14:20,870
Well, this is bad.

143
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:22,740
There's a scratch right here.

144
00:14:23,490 --> 00:14:24,970
Looks like you owe me some cash, huh?

145
00:14:25,630 --> 00:14:26,830
Hold on, that scratch...

146
00:14:28,050 --> 00:14:30,010
You put that there yourself
just now, didn't you?

147
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:34,290
Are you seriously accusing
a customer right now?

148
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:39,480
Now my feelings are hurt,
right along with my car.

149
00:14:39,890 --> 00:14:41,976
You're gonna have to pay
for my emotional distress, too.

150
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,600
Cough up the money, bastard!

151
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:46,900
Oh, man.

152
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,790
Look at the rear end
on this beauty. Gorgeous.

153
00:14:51,010 --> 00:14:52,010
Huh?

154
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:53,850
Pops,

155
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:55,610
your craftsmanship is top-notch.

156
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:00,470
With an eye for detail like yours,

157
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:03,250
there's no way you'd just
leave a scratch like that.

158
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,640
Anyone can see that a mile away.

159
00:15:05,370 --> 00:15:06,370
Excuse me?

160
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,990
Mind your own damn business, pal.

161
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:09,710
- Bro! - What?!

162
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:11,190
That guy...

163
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,720
He's the second-in-command
of the Kirii-gumi.

164
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,079
Wait, for real?

165
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,290
Crap, let's get out of here!

166
00:15:15,950 --> 00:15:16,850
Sorry to bother you!

167
00:15:16,910 --> 00:15:17,850
Hey, move it!

168
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:20,100
Sorry about that, please
take good care of the car!

169
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:22,850
- Hey, wait for me!
- Don't let the door hit you on the way out.

170
00:15:25,590 --> 00:15:28,510
Driving a ride like this every once
in a while wouldn't be half bad, huh?

171
00:15:30,050 --> 00:15:31,250
Name your price. I'll take it.

172
00:15:36,710 --> 00:15:37,710
Here's a deposit.

173
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:40,180
- Uh, wait... - I'll be back.

174
00:15:48,210 --> 00:15:49,570
He really is an incredible guy.

175
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:53,260
Anyone who meets young Kataoka...

176
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:55,010
can't help but be drawn to him.

177
00:15:59,510 --> 00:16:00,510
That's true.

178
00:16:02,490 --> 00:16:04,930
Looks like you're trying to
track down the owner of that van,

179
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:06,930
but that's just a delivery vehicle.

180
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:09,660
And the owner's no kid, either.

181
00:16:11,190 --> 00:16:12,190
That said...

182
00:16:12,590 --> 00:16:13,710
I do know a gang of punks...

183
00:16:14,530 --> 00:16:16,760
who are always cruising
around in the exact same model.

184
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:18,520
Please!

185
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:20,570
Tell us everything you know about them.

186
00:16:24,710 --> 00:16:25,810
All right.

187
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,880
I'll tell you where they hang
out. You can go check it out.

188
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:46,350
That must be the van
the old man told us about.

189
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,600
Those bastards...

190
00:17:00,070 --> 00:17:01,070
I'll go in alone.

191
00:17:01,870 --> 00:17:02,870
Odajima-san?

192
00:17:04,610 --> 00:17:05,610
If anything goes south,

193
00:17:05,810 --> 00:17:07,160
call Boss Kumakura immediately.

194
00:17:07,390 --> 00:17:08,390
Odajima-san...

195
00:17:10,210 --> 00:17:12,280
This is a really bad idea!

196
00:17:58,670 --> 00:17:59,970
Where is he?

197
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:16,630
What the hell are you doing?! Hey!

198
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:51,180
That guy...

199
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:53,860
I bet he's doing something reckless again.

200
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:06,940
Did you get it all out of your system, kid?

201
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,040
Man, you've got some serious fire in you.

202
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,180
From the very beginning, I was just...

203
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,560
a mistake who never should've been born...

204
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:22,070
into this world anyway.

205
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:24,330
So naturally, my life...

206
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,950
has no meaning at all.

207
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,040
Don't push it.

208
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:44,800
Odajima.

209
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:18,900
That's enough!

210
00:20:19,090 --> 00:20:20,090
Hold on.

211
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:29,880
Since you're dying to see him so badly,

212
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:31,320
I'll grant your wish.

213
00:20:58,560 --> 00:20:59,760
Odajima-san...

214
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,660
I hope he's okay...

215
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:36,220
Odajima-san.

216
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,040
This is bad.

217
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,930
They're on the move.

218
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,200
Did he take the bait?

219
00:22:44,260 --> 00:22:45,460
That was fast.

220
00:23:00,730 --> 00:23:02,729
Everything is...

221
00:23:02,730 --> 00:23:04,030
right in the palm of my hand.

222
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:32,870
(Next Episode Preview)

223
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:34,800
You actually risked your
neck to come after me.

224
00:23:35,370 --> 00:23:37,170
Did you miss me that much?

225
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:38,680
If I wanted to see you,

226
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:40,240
this was the only way.

227
00:23:40,630 --> 00:23:42,870
I told you, I have no
obligation to get involved.

228
00:23:43,250 --> 00:23:44,530
If we let a civilian get killed,

229
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:46,280
it'd be a disgrace to our family.

230
00:23:47,130 --> 00:23:48,130
Boss.

231
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,460
You think you're pulling all the strings,

232
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:52,826
when you're really just
being played for a fool.

233
00:23:52,850 --> 00:23:53,850
I have never once...

234
00:23:54,180 --> 00:23:57,320
thought about leaving your side.

235
00:23:57,560 --> 00:24:01,350
Never underestimate the
resolve of an ex-yakuza!
